WEBVTT

00:00:17.007 --> 00:00:19.840
It is the summer of 1945...

00:00:19.877 --> 00:00:21.845
31/2 years after the war...

00:00:21.879 --> 00:00:24.348
between Japan
and the Allies began.

00:00:24.381 --> 00:00:26.008
Despite initial successes...

00:00:26.050 --> 00:00:28.018
the Japanese have seen
the tide of battle...

00:00:28.052 --> 00:00:29.486
turn against them.

00:00:29.520 --> 00:00:33.013
The Americans have leapfrogged
across the Pacific...

00:00:33.057 --> 00:00:36.516
sweeping the Japanese
before them.

00:00:36.560 --> 00:00:39.029
Japan's Imperial fleet
has been neutralized...

00:00:39.063 --> 00:00:40.531
its air force overpowered.

00:00:40.564 --> 00:00:43.534
From the island air bases
they now control...

00:00:43.567 --> 00:00:46.434
the Americans' B-29
Flying Fortresses...

00:00:46.470 --> 00:00:49.531
are able to strike
at the Japanese home islands.

00:00:49.573 --> 00:00:52.440
A systematic
fire-bombing campaign...

00:00:52.476 --> 00:00:54.774
is launched against cities
and industrial centers.

00:00:54.812 --> 00:00:57.042
It is the most devastating
attack...

00:00:57.081 --> 00:00:58.640
against civilian targets
ever carried out.

00:01:02.586 --> 00:01:05.055
Meanwhile, in America...

00:01:05.089 --> 00:01:06.887
Robert Oppenheimer
and other scientists...

00:01:06.924 --> 00:01:09.552
have spent three years
working in secrecy...

00:01:09.593 --> 00:01:11.493
to develop a new type of bomb.

00:01:11.528 --> 00:01:13.223
They have at last succeeded.

00:01:13.263 --> 00:01:15.061
But their achievement is not yet
known to the world...

00:01:15.099 --> 00:01:17.067
and certainly not
to the citizens of Hiroshima...

00:01:17.101 --> 00:01:18.296
in the summer of 1945.

00:01:28.112 --> 00:01:30.240
All clear!

00:01:30.280 --> 00:01:32.578
The enemy has gone!

00:01:32.616 --> 00:01:36.109
All clear!

00:01:36.153 --> 00:01:38.679
We

00:01:38.722 --> 00:01:40.816
All clear!

00:01:53.137 --> 00:01:55.868
- I'm still hungry.
- I am,too.

00:01:55.906 --> 00:01:58.102
We've got work to do first.

00:01:59.143 --> 00:02:02.113
Father, is this wheat
almost ready for harvesting?

00:02:02.146 --> 00:02:05.116
I can't wait.
I'm gonna eat so much bread!

00:02:05.149 --> 00:02:07.811
Bread and bread and bread
until I throw up.

00:02:07.851 --> 00:02:10.912
Noodles! I'm gonna eat
noodles till I burst!

00:02:10.954 --> 00:02:13.582
- Gen.
- Uh-huh?

00:02:13.624 --> 00:02:15.592
- Shinji.
- Yep?

00:02:15.626 --> 00:02:17.094
Look at it, boys.

00:02:17.127 --> 00:02:21.086
Its life begins in
the coldest season of the year.

00:02:21.131 --> 00:02:24.101
The rain pounds it,
the wind blows it...

00:02:24.134 --> 00:02:26.603
it's crushed
beneath people's feet...

00:02:26.637 --> 00:02:29.265
but still the wheat
spreads its roots and grows.

00:02:29.306 --> 00:02:30.671
It survives.

00:02:30.707 --> 00:02:33.369
So, let the wheat
be an example to you, my boys.

00:02:33.410 --> 00:02:34.536
Rig ht?

00:02:34.578 --> 00:02:36.444
We're sick of
that dumb ol' story.

00:02:36.480 --> 00:02:37.948
Sick of it, are you?

00:02:37.981 --> 00:02:40.951
- Yay!
- Yay!

00:02:42.586 --> 00:02:44.680
Ha ha ha ha ha!

00:02:44.721 --> 00:02:48.351
- Yay!
- Yay!

00:02:48.392 --> 00:02:52.329
'AYee!
'AYee!

00:02:53.330 --> 00:02:54.820
<i>Kw“! am '!</i>

00:04:17.648 --> 00:04:19.878
You do my mother and me
great honor by coming here...

00:04:19.916 --> 00:04:22.578
and wishing me well
in my service to the emperor.

00:04:22.619 --> 00:04:25.611
Fight bravely, Oyama. Banzai!

00:05:01.692 --> 00:05:03.854
I'm off to join the army now...

00:05:03.894 --> 00:05:05.419
You get filthy blanket...

00:05:05.462 --> 00:05:07.294
Their dishes
are made of metal...

00:05:07.331 --> 00:05:09.095
So are the chopsticks...

00:05:09.132 --> 00:05:12.693
One small scoop of rice
in a tiny bowl...

00:05:12.736 --> 00:05:16.764
A bowl of rotten rice
with some bugs on top.

00:05:16.807 --> 00:05:19.777
I'm hungry.
I'm so hungry I'm dizzy.

00:05:19.810 --> 00:05:21.278
I'm so hungry--

00:05:21.311 --> 00:05:23.643
I could eat a whole goat!

00:05:23.680 --> 00:05:27.275
If you've got a ration stamp,
today's your lucky day.

00:05:27.317 --> 00:05:29.945
The soup's even got
rice in it today.

00:05:32.823 --> 00:05:34.655
Look at that!

00:05:34.691 --> 00:05:37.353
I haven't seen
this much rice in weeks!

00:05:44.468 --> 00:05:45.799
Hey!

00:05:45.836 --> 00:05:48.828
Father,
can we have some soup, too?

00:05:50.474 --> 00:05:53.307
I'm sorry, boys. Not today.
There's no more ration stamps.

00:05:53.343 --> 00:05:54.811
You'll just have to be patient.

00:05:54.845 --> 00:05:57.143
- We're hungry.
- We're starving.

00:05:57.180 --> 00:05:58.807
Get outta my way!

00:05:58.849 --> 00:06:00.817
What makes you think
you can cut in line?

00:06:00.851 --> 00:06:03.183
- You wait your turn, or I'll--
- What?

00:06:05.489 --> 00:06:07.821
Who made you soup monitor, huh?

00:06:07.858 --> 00:06:10.623
- How dare you?
- Get him!

00:06:10.660 --> 00:06:13.994
Hit him hard right in--Wait!

00:06:14.031 --> 00:06:15.999
Isn't that terrible, Father?

00:06:16.033 --> 00:06:19.003
Grown men fighting over
a bowl of soup.

00:06:19.036 --> 00:06:21.869
If they're gonna fight,
it should be over some fish.

00:06:24.007 --> 00:06:25.975
Mother! We're home!

00:06:26.009 --> 00:06:27.841
We're back!

00:06:27.878 --> 00:06:31.508
Did you miss us?

00:06:31.548 --> 00:06:33.846
What's to eat? I'm starving.

00:06:33.884 --> 00:06:36.012
There might be something.
Let's see.

00:06:44.394 --> 00:06:48.422
You were hiding something
up there, weren't you?

00:06:48.465 --> 00:06:49.864
Sweet potato!

00:06:49.900 --> 00:06:52.369
Wait a minute, Shinji.
Aren't ya gonna share it?

00:06:52.402 --> 00:06:54.427
- No!
- Come back here!

00:06:54.471 --> 00:06:56.940
It's not yours!

00:06:56.973 --> 00:06:58.873
No! You'll just eat it all!

00:06:58.909 --> 00:07:01.344
Gimme it! I'm not kidding!

00:07:01.378 --> 00:07:03.847
No! No! No'
'Shinji! '

00:07:03.880 --> 00:07:06.349
Who do you think you are,
you little runt?

00:07:06.383 --> 00:07:08.875
- Come here!
- No! Get away!

00:07:08.919 --> 00:07:11.183
That does it! Stop!

00:07:12.889 --> 00:07:13.879
Stay awfly!

00:07:13.924 --> 00:07:16.222
We're supposed to share,
and you know it.

00:07:16.259 --> 00:07:18.387
Don't you dare!

00:07:18.428 --> 00:07:20.624
Give it to me!
You're gonna get it!

00:07:24.134 --> 00:07:25.226
Ow!

00:07:25.268 --> 00:07:27.100
Shinji, you're such a...

00:07:29.773 --> 00:07:31.002
Brat!

00:07:37.948 --> 00:07:39.939
You're gonna be so sorry!

00:07:42.486 --> 00:07:45.012
OK. Now give it!

00:07:50.160 --> 00:07:52.959
Hey. That's mine.
Give it, Eiko.

00:07:52.996 --> 00:07:55.966
You know that this is
supposed to be for her.

00:07:55.999 --> 00:07:59.492
- What do you mean, for her?
- Why'd she give it to us?

00:07:59.536 --> 00:08:00.935
She was just being nice.

00:08:00.971 --> 00:08:04.430
Mother needs to be strong
for the baby that's coming.

00:08:04.474 --> 00:08:07.500
If you eat this potato,
the baby will die.

00:08:07.544 --> 00:08:10.343
Now, do you both still want it?

00:08:10.380 --> 00:08:12.439
Eiko, go on,
it's all right, dear.

00:08:12.482 --> 00:08:14.280
Let your brothers have it.

00:08:14.317 --> 00:08:15.614
But, Mother, it's not fair.

00:08:15.652 --> 00:08:17.450
The baby needs it
more than they do.

00:08:17.487 --> 00:08:18.977
Here. You take it.

00:08:20.991 --> 00:08:23.050
Please, eat it for the baby.

00:08:32.502 --> 00:08:35.563
Stop it, you two. Come on.
You'll get something later.

00:08:39.543 --> 00:08:41.978
You know, dear,
it's a terrible thing...

00:08:42.012 --> 00:08:44.982
having to watch
children go hungry.

00:08:45.015 --> 00:08:47.985
And what's worse, there's hardly
any food to be bought...

00:08:48.018 --> 00:08:49.611
even if we had the money.

00:08:49.653 --> 00:08:51.985
We'll just have
to be patient, that's all.

00:08:52.022 --> 00:08:54.548
- Ah!
- What?

00:08:54.591 --> 00:08:57.993
Don't worry. It's just our baby
moving around in there.

00:08:58.028 --> 00:08:59.553
It tickled me.

00:08:59.596 --> 00:09:01.997
What, again? You know what
that means, don't you?

00:09:02.032 --> 00:09:03.557
It's strong--a healthy one.

00:09:03.600 --> 00:09:06.570
It's a healthy one, all--Ooh!

00:09:06.603 --> 00:09:09.163
It's got spirit.

00:09:09.206 --> 00:09:10.537
What're you laughing at?

00:09:10.574 --> 00:09:13.441
The baby's moving.
It wants to come out.

00:09:13.476 --> 00:09:16.241
It's moving? But how?
It hasn't been born yet.

00:09:24.054 --> 00:09:26.022
It moved again.

00:09:26.056 --> 00:09:28.024
That's funny. You know what?

00:09:28.058 --> 00:09:30.026
I think it must be a boy.

00:09:30.060 --> 00:09:32.154
You can never tell
until it's born.

00:09:32.195 --> 00:09:34.357
Well, I can't wait.

00:09:34.397 --> 00:09:38.027
Oh, you just want another
little brother to boss around.

00:09:38.068 --> 00:09:40.196
Well, you can't
have this one, Gen...

00:09:40.237 --> 00:09:43.366
I cause if it's a boy,
he's gonna be my little brother.

00:09:43.406 --> 00:09:45.875
So I suppose you'll
boss him around...

00:09:45.909 --> 00:09:47.707
and I'd hate to think
what you'll teach him.

00:09:47.744 --> 00:09:49.371
It'd frighten me half to death.

00:09:49.412 --> 00:09:52.712
Ha! See?
You'd be a bad example.

00:09:54.751 --> 00:09:56.617
No, I wouldn't.

00:09:56.653 --> 00:09:58.621
I didn't mean it.

00:09:58.655 --> 00:10:01.124
I was only joking.

00:10:01.157 --> 00:10:03.125
You're a good boy, Shinji.

00:10:03.159 --> 00:10:05.753
I know you'll be
a good brother to the baby.

00:10:12.669 --> 00:10:14.398
When's it coming?

00:10:14.437 --> 00:10:17.771
Come out, little brother.
Hurry it up.

00:10:44.534 --> 00:10:46.662
Children, wake up!

00:10:46.703 --> 00:10:49.104
Attention! Attention!
Air raid!

00:10:49.139 --> 00:10:50.607
Go to your shelters at once!

00:10:50.640 --> 00:10:53.132
Air raid! To your shelters!

00:10:54.277 --> 00:10:57.247
Everyone in the shelter.
Eiko, bring your brothers.

00:10:57.280 --> 00:10:59.112
Oh, no.

00:10:59.149 --> 00:11:01.140
Come on, Gen. We've got to go.

00:11:02.385 --> 00:11:04.285
Wake Shinji up. Come on.

00:11:04.321 --> 00:11:06.255
Shinji, come on.

00:11:07.557 --> 00:11:10.549
Just leave him to me, Eiko.
I'll wake him up.

00:11:16.066 --> 00:11:17.465
Wowwvv! Rice, Shinji!

00:11:17.500 --> 00:11:18.763
Look at it all!

00:11:18.802 --> 00:11:21.100
And see? Noodles--lots of 'em!

00:11:21.137 --> 00:11:22.263
Where?

00:11:22.305 --> 00:11:23.466
Real noodles?

00:11:23.506 --> 00:11:24.974
Hey. What's going on?

00:11:25.008 --> 00:11:26.476
This bowl's empty!

00:11:26.509 --> 00:11:28.773
You ate 'em all!

00:11:33.550 --> 00:11:35.484
We're supposed to share.

00:11:35.518 --> 00:11:36.644
Get off!

00:11:36.686 --> 00:11:38.154
Share what?

00:11:38.188 --> 00:11:40.054
The noodles.

00:11:41.191 --> 00:11:43.023
What is going on here?

00:11:46.529 --> 00:11:47.655
Dunno.

00:11:47.697 --> 00:11:49.096
What are we doing?

00:12:07.217 --> 00:12:08.707
Hurry up, boy-

00:12:09.753 --> 00:12:11.687
Suppose you want one
to land on your head...

00:12:11.721 --> 00:12:13.712
is that what you want?

00:12:13.757 --> 00:12:16.226
Bet it's just another spy plane.

00:12:16.259 --> 00:12:18.694
They never drop bombs on us.
We're too boring.

00:12:18.728 --> 00:12:20.218
How can you say that?

00:12:20.263 --> 00:12:23.631
Have you forgotten the child
from the 400 block who was shot?

00:12:50.760 --> 00:12:52.228
Tokyo, Yokohama, Nagoya,
Osaka...

00:12:52.262 --> 00:12:54.230
They've come against
all the big cities...

00:12:54.264 --> 00:12:55.993
and bombed them into ruins.

00:12:56.032 --> 00:12:59.991
It's serious, Gen. I won't
have you making light of it.

00:13:00.036 --> 00:13:02.505
There's one thing
that bothers me.

00:13:03.540 --> 00:13:06.737
It's like you said,
every major city around us...

00:13:06.776 --> 00:13:09.336
has been bombed over and over
again, but never Hiroshima.

00:13:13.950 --> 00:13:18.080
The enemy has gone!
All clear! The enemy has gone!

00:13:18.121 --> 00:13:20.522
Ha! Told ya!

00:13:20.557 --> 00:13:21.683
All clear!

00:13:21.724 --> 00:13:25.183
Return to your homes!

00:13:25.228 --> 00:13:27.424
I knew it was just a spy plane.

00:13:27.463 --> 00:13:30.125
So I had to wake up and
get out of bed for nothing?

00:13:36.172 --> 00:13:38.266
All safe and sound--Ohh!

00:13:38.308 --> 00:13:41.141
Mother! Are you all right?
Is it the baby?

00:13:41.177 --> 00:13:43.145
Kimei, what's wrong?

00:13:44.681 --> 00:13:45.773
Just a little dizzy.

00:13:45.815 --> 00:13:48.113
- Kimei!
- Mother!

00:13:48.151 --> 00:13:50.279
Boys, go fetch the doctor!

00:13:50.320 --> 00:13:51.446
Rig ht!

00:13:51.487 --> 00:13:54.286
- Eiko, make up the bed.
- Yes, Father.

00:13:54.324 --> 00:13:57.294
Kimei, hang on.
It won't belong.

00:13:57.327 --> 00:14:00.319
The doctor should
be coming in no time.

00:14:03.333 --> 00:14:05.665
Hey, Gen, is Mother gonna die?

00:14:05.702 --> 00:14:08.296
Oh, no!
Mother's dying, isn't she?

00:14:08.338 --> 00:14:12.002
Shinji, shut up!
Mother's not going to die.

00:14:27.090 --> 00:14:28.717
Wake up, Doctor! Wake up!

00:14:28.758 --> 00:14:30.556
Our mother needs help!

00:14:30.593 --> 00:14:32.561
Hurry up!
It's really important!

00:14:32.595 --> 00:14:35.462
She's got my little brother
in her tummy!

00:14:37.767 --> 00:14:39.326
Slow down, boys. Slow down.

00:14:39.369 --> 00:14:42.339
I'll die of a heart attack
before we get there.

00:14:42.372 --> 00:14:44.340
You should've thought of that
before you got so fat.

00:14:44.374 --> 00:14:45.808
Our mother's sick, and if you
don't make her better...

00:14:45.842 --> 00:14:47.003
you'll be sorry.

00:14:53.082 --> 00:14:54.345
Will she be all right?

00:14:54.384 --> 00:14:57.354
She's suffering from
severe malnutrition.

00:14:57.387 --> 00:15:00.846
If she gets plenty to eat,
her strength will return...

00:15:00.890 --> 00:15:02.551
and she should be fine.

00:15:04.060 --> 00:15:07.030
Of course,
that's easier said than done.

00:15:07.063 --> 00:15:11.523
It seems we don't have enough
food or medicine for anybody.

00:15:11.567 --> 00:15:13.296
I'm sorry.

00:15:16.272 --> 00:15:18.536
This is serious.
We've got to do something.

00:15:18.575 --> 00:15:21.670
This is really serious.
We've really gotta do something.

00:16:03.119 --> 00:16:06.419
What is it, Eiko?
What's the matter?

00:16:06.456 --> 00:16:10.916
It's just that the last of
the rice is gone, Father...

00:16:10.960 --> 00:16:13.725
and we have no money
to buy any more.

00:16:13.763 --> 00:16:15.925
Don't worry.
Something will come along.

00:16:15.965 --> 00:16:17.296
We'll find the money.

00:16:17.333 --> 00:16:20.928
We just have to keep at it
and finish our work.

00:16:20.970 --> 00:16:23.302
Then maybe we'll get paid
what we're owed.

00:16:23.339 --> 00:16:26.798
Eiko, you mustn't overdo it.
You're not very strong.

00:16:26.843 --> 00:16:29.312
Oh, I'm all right.

00:16:30.480 --> 00:16:31.811
I'm sure.

00:16:55.004 --> 00:16:56.301
Hey. Come here, Gen.

00:16:56.339 --> 00:16:57.670
What is it?

00:16:57.707 --> 00:16:59.801
Has anybody ever eaten a worm?

00:16:59.842 --> 00:17:01.173
Eaten a worm?

00:17:01.210 --> 00:17:02.678
Like a caterpillar?

00:17:02.712 --> 00:17:04.680
I don't know.

00:17:04.714 --> 00:17:08.344
If they won't make you sick,
then Mother could eat them.

00:17:15.224 --> 00:17:16.487
Idiot!

00:17:16.526 --> 00:17:19.188
Good morning, boys.
I heard noises last night.

00:17:19.228 --> 00:17:20.354
Hi,Mr. Pak.

00:17:20.396 --> 00:17:22.160
Everything all right?
Has the baby come?

00:17:22.198 --> 00:17:23.666
Our mother's sick.

00:17:23.699 --> 00:17:26.669
The doctor,
he said she's got malnutrition.

00:17:26.703 --> 00:17:29.001
That's terrible, and just when
she needs all her strength.

00:17:29.038 --> 00:17:32.497
Somebody once told me carp's
blood is the best thing...

00:17:32.542 --> 00:17:34.670
for a woman in her condition.

00:17:34.711 --> 00:17:36.679
Huh?

00:17:36.713 --> 00:17:39.182
Carp? Like the fish?

00:17:39.215 --> 00:17:40.376
Yeah?

00:17:47.857 --> 00:17:51.521
Gee, I sure didn't know any of
that stuff about carp's blood.

00:17:51.561 --> 00:17:54.326
If we could catch one for her,
Mother would get all better.

00:17:55.365 --> 00:17:56.833
So, let's do it!

00:17:56.866 --> 00:17:58.334
Yes, sir!

00:18:01.571 --> 00:18:02.697
Sergeant!

00:18:02.739 --> 00:18:04.207
Captain!

00:18:04.240 --> 00:18:05.708
Move out!

00:18:05.742 --> 00:18:07.301
Company, forward!

00:18:41.778 --> 00:18:42.904
Rats!

00:18:42.945 --> 00:18:44.071
Hold still!

00:18:44.113 --> 00:18:45.274
Move over!

00:18:47.450 --> 00:18:50.078
Look, Shinji.
Look at all the carp.

00:18:50.119 --> 00:18:51.587
And they're so big.

00:18:51.621 --> 00:18:54.090
Scan the perimeter, Sergeant.
Any sign of the enemy?

00:18:55.958 --> 00:18:58.052
Negative, sir.

00:19:01.464 --> 00:19:03.296
Hey! Look! Look!

00:19:04.467 --> 00:19:06.435
I think I caught one.

00:19:06.469 --> 00:19:08.096
That was fast.
He must be hungry, too.

00:19:08.137 --> 00:19:11.630
He almost pulled me in!

00:19:14.510 --> 00:19:16.410
He's a big one!

00:19:16.446 --> 00:19:17.845
Really big!

00:19:17.880 --> 00:19:20.110
Hang on, Shinji. Don't let go.

00:19:20.149 --> 00:19:21.344
I won't.

00:19:21.384 --> 00:19:22.852
I'm going in after it.

00:19:41.370 --> 00:19:43.338
Got him, Shinji! See?

00:19:43.372 --> 00:19:45.864
I can't believe it! Victory!

00:19:48.678 --> 00:19:50.772
Now let's take him home.

00:19:50.813 --> 00:19:53.373
Don't forget to tell Father
who caught it.

00:19:58.020 --> 00:19:59.385
Get out of here!

00:20:02.892 --> 00:20:04.951
Dirty little thieves!

00:20:05.895 --> 00:20:07.090
Let go of that fish!

00:20:11.901 --> 00:20:13.369
You hit Gen!

00:20:20.977 --> 00:20:22.877
You can hit me again, sir.

00:20:22.912 --> 00:20:26.348
Really, you can hit me
as much as you like.

00:20:26.382 --> 00:20:30.842
Go on, but just let us keep
the fish when you're done.

00:20:30.887 --> 00:20:32.218
Please, sir.

00:20:33.322 --> 00:20:34.448
That's rig ht!

00:20:34.490 --> 00:20:37.016
You can hit me as much
as you want, too.

00:20:37.059 --> 00:20:38.185
But give us the fish.

00:20:38.227 --> 00:20:39.717
Go on. I'm ready.

00:20:51.807 --> 00:20:55.038
Will you tell me why you boys
want that blasted carp?

00:20:55.077 --> 00:20:56.545
It's for our mother, sir.

00:20:56.579 --> 00:20:58.547
She's going to have a baby,
and she's not very well.

00:20:58.581 --> 00:21:02.484
And Mr. Pak said carp blood's
the only thing that'll help her.

00:21:05.588 --> 00:21:08.421
Without it, my mother
will get worse or even--

00:21:08.457 --> 00:21:11.483
You wouldn't want my mother
to die, would you?

00:21:14.597 --> 00:21:16.565
Oh, please, help us.

00:21:16.599 --> 00:21:18.499
Please save her.

00:21:23.773 --> 00:21:24.934
You won't?

00:21:26.943 --> 00:21:28.570
Oh, no!

00:21:29.579 --> 00:21:32.810
You're a mean old fart,
aren't you?

00:21:32.848 --> 00:21:37.809
Her ghost will come back
and haunt you till you die!

00:21:45.928 --> 00:21:48.397
How does the old saying go?

00:21:48.431 --> 00:21:50.923
Be good to your parents
while you can.

00:21:53.135 --> 00:21:54.534
Very well. Keep it.

00:21:58.307 --> 00:22:01.277
Take the carp along
to your mother, please.

00:22:01.310 --> 00:22:03.278
You mean it, really?

00:22:03.312 --> 00:22:06.282
Remember, old man, if you lie,
you'll go straight to hell.

00:22:06.315 --> 00:22:10.081
Funny, I was just about to say
the same thing to you two.

00:22:38.881 --> 00:22:41.851
If you boys stole it, you know
just what I'll do to you.

00:22:41.884 --> 00:22:44.319
We didn't.
The old man gave it to us.

00:22:44.353 --> 00:22:45.843
Don't you believe us?

00:22:45.888 --> 00:22:47.822
Cook it and give it to Mother.

00:22:47.857 --> 00:22:50.326
It's the best thing for a woman
in her condition.

00:22:50.359 --> 00:22:53.795
Hurry up and cook it--now.

00:22:55.531 --> 00:22:58.364
Eiko, you heard him.

00:22:58.401 --> 00:22:59.800
OK.

00:23:15.885 --> 00:23:18.855
Will Mother get better now?

00:23:18.888 --> 00:23:21.585
I hope she will.

00:23:21.624 --> 00:23:24.355
You boys shouldn't have
to worry about such things.

00:23:24.393 --> 00:23:26.521
I'll just have to work harder.

00:23:26.562 --> 00:23:29.827
I'd like to know
if we'll ever have enough food.

00:23:29.865 --> 00:23:30.991
Will we?

00:23:31.033 --> 00:23:34.333
Yes, son, when the war is over.

00:23:34.370 --> 00:23:36.236
When will it be over?

00:23:36.272 --> 00:23:40.266
It won't belong.
Japan has all but lost the war.

00:23:40.309 --> 00:23:43.279
Why do we keep on fighting
if we've lost the war?

00:23:43.312 --> 00:23:46.282
Why? Because our government
is run by madmen.

00:23:46.315 --> 00:23:48.784
They're just stupid, crazy.
All of them.

00:23:48.818 --> 00:23:51.287
Father, you shouldn't
say stuff like that.

00:23:51.320 --> 00:23:53.516
They might call you
a traitor or something.

00:23:53.556 --> 00:23:55.786
Traitor, coward--
those words mean nothing to me.

00:23:55.825 --> 00:23:57.793
Actually, come to think of it...

00:23:57.827 --> 00:23:59.556
I'm proud if they want
to call me those things.

00:24:00.830 --> 00:24:02.798
This war can't be right...

00:24:02.832 --> 00:24:06.791
but it's only the cowards
like me who dare say it.

00:24:06.836 --> 00:24:09.305
If there were
only a few more like us.

00:24:09.338 --> 00:24:11.306
You know, sometimes it takes
more courage...

00:24:11.340 --> 00:24:14.799
not to fight than to fight,
to not want to kill...

00:24:14.844 --> 00:24:17.176
when all around you
are calling out for blood.

00:24:17.213 --> 00:24:19.705
That's real courage in my book.

00:24:19.749 --> 00:24:22.719
If you boys remember nothing
else that I teach you...

00:24:22.752 --> 00:24:25.653
I hope you'll remember that,
all right?

00:24:29.458 --> 00:24:32.519
- Hey, Father?
- What is it?

00:24:32.561 --> 00:24:34.325
I just wanted to say
I love you, Father.

00:24:34.363 --> 00:24:37.333
Yeah, I want to say
I love you, too, Father.

00:24:37.366 --> 00:24:38.527
I know.

00:24:40.536 --> 00:24:42.504
Are you sure you don't mind?

00:24:42.538 --> 00:24:45.439
I should be sharing this
with all of you.

00:24:45.474 --> 00:24:46.942
Don't be silly, Mother.

00:24:46.976 --> 00:24:49.445
You're not well,
and you're eating for two now.

00:24:49.478 --> 00:24:51.173
You're right.

00:24:51.213 --> 00:24:52.681
Well, how is it?

00:24:52.715 --> 00:24:54.877
It's delicious.

00:24:59.221 --> 00:25:01.189
Why the big grin, son?

00:25:01.223 --> 00:25:03.590
A secret.

00:25:18.240 --> 00:25:21.039
Shinji, what did you say
to make Mother cry?

00:25:21.077 --> 00:25:23.910
All I did was ask if I could
suck on the fish bones...

00:25:23.946 --> 00:25:25.539
when she was done with them.

00:25:25.581 --> 00:25:27.208
You're kidding.
You asked her that?

00:25:27.249 --> 00:25:29.616
- Yeah, that was it.
- Idiot!

00:25:29.652 --> 00:25:33.748
What was that for? How come
you're always hitting me?

00:25:33.789 --> 00:25:35.553
Hurry up, Shinji. Come on.

00:25:35.591 --> 00:25:39.050
You big bully, Gen. Father!

00:25:39.094 --> 00:25:42.223
Eiko! Eiko!

00:25:42.264 --> 00:25:44.062
Yes, Mr. Pa k?

00:25:44.099 --> 00:25:47.729
I brought a little something
for you and your family.

00:25:47.770 --> 00:25:48.931
Take it.

00:25:50.105 --> 00:25:53.006
- Rice!
- It isn't much.

00:25:54.109 --> 00:25:55.270
Mr. Pak...

00:25:57.446 --> 00:25:58.936
Thank you.

00:26:02.117 --> 00:26:05.087
We sure did a good job getting
that carp, didn't we?

00:26:05.120 --> 00:26:08.613
Yeah, Mother'll be
all better again in no time.

00:26:09.625 --> 00:26:11.525
Hello, is anybody home?

00:26:23.072 --> 00:26:27.009
Never thought that old grouch
would come to our house.

00:26:27.042 --> 00:26:29.272
I bet he's gonna
tell Father all about...

00:26:29.311 --> 00:26:31.279
how we tried to steal his carp.

00:26:31.313 --> 00:26:33.281
<i>Father“ get mad, won't he?</i>

00:26:33.315 --> 00:26:36.012
I had no idea. I'm sorry.

00:26:36.051 --> 00:26:39.885
The boys will be punished, sir.
I assure you.

00:26:39.922 --> 00:26:42.892
Oh, no, please.
You misunderstood me.

00:26:42.925 --> 00:26:45.019
I didn't come here for that.

00:26:45.060 --> 00:26:47.529
I admire the boys.
Such high spirits.

00:26:47.563 --> 00:26:50.032
Such devotion
to you and their mother.

00:26:50.065 --> 00:26:52.534
You have good sons there,
Nakaoka.

00:26:52.568 --> 00:26:54.536
I envy you...

00:26:54.570 --> 00:26:58.370
though I'm sure they're
quite a handful at times.

00:26:58.407 --> 00:26:59.875
What'll we do?

00:26:59.909 --> 00:27:02.879
What do you think?
Prepare to get hit.

00:27:02.912 --> 00:27:05.381
He wouldn't do that, would he?

00:27:05.414 --> 00:27:08.213
- There you are.
- Shinji.

00:27:08.250 --> 00:27:09.809
Well, then?

00:27:09.852 --> 00:27:12.082
Come in and sit down.

00:27:37.379 --> 00:27:39.438
Told ya.

00:27:44.186 --> 00:27:51.354
Never thought I'd be getting
a piece of cake out of this.

00:27:51.393 --> 00:27:53.862
Hey, we did good, right?

00:27:53.896 --> 00:27:55.261
Yeah.

00:27:55.297 --> 00:27:58.358
That old fisherman
is not so bad after all.

00:27:58.400 --> 00:28:00.368
I ought to let him
join our platoon.

00:28:00.402 --> 00:28:02.564
I might give him a medal.

00:28:13.415 --> 00:28:16.385
At 2:45 a.m.,
three American B-29s took off...

00:28:16.418 --> 00:28:18.386
from an air base on Tinian
in the Marianas.

00:28:18.420 --> 00:28:20.388
Two of them
were observation planes.

00:28:20.422 --> 00:28:21.890
The third was the Enola Gay...

00:28:21.924 --> 00:28:23.517
named after
the captain's mother.

00:28:26.428 --> 00:28:31.127
Mother, leave the washing to me.
You're still not well.

00:28:31.166 --> 00:28:35.660
It's OK. If I rest too long,
I'm liable to get lazy.

00:28:35.704 --> 00:28:38.173
Father, isn't this the greatest
boat you ever saw?

00:28:38.207 --> 00:28:40.676
- Gen made it for me!
- Did he really?

00:28:40.709 --> 00:28:43.178
The minute
he's home from school...

00:28:43.212 --> 00:28:45.146
we're going to take it
to the river.

00:28:45.180 --> 00:28:48.810
Are you? Won't that be fun?

00:28:48.851 --> 00:28:51.684
Enemy planes again?
It's so early.

00:29:06.702 --> 00:29:08.170
All clear!

00:29:08.203 --> 00:29:10.672
The enemy has gone!

00:29:10.706 --> 00:29:14.643
All clear! The enemy has gone!

00:29:14.677 --> 00:29:16.645
Another spy plane, I betcha.

00:29:16.678 --> 00:29:20.137
Well, that's a B-29 vapor trail.

00:29:20.182 --> 00:29:22.583
Look how clear the sky is.

00:29:22.618 --> 00:29:24.347
It'll be hot today.

00:29:24.386 --> 00:29:27.356
Weather observation plane
Easerly calling Enola Gay.

00:29:27.389 --> 00:29:28.857
Calling Enola Gay.

00:29:28.891 --> 00:29:30.723
Weatherfls fair and clear
over Hiroshima.

00:29:30.759 --> 00:29:32.454
Conditions favorable
for bombing.

00:29:32.494 --> 00:29:36.727
Roger. Enola Gay getting ready
to drop on target.

00:29:44.707 --> 00:29:48.666
I better get going or
I'll be late for school.

00:29:48.710 --> 00:29:50.678
You're coming right home
after school, OK?

00:29:50.712 --> 00:29:52.680
We're going down
to the river, right?

00:29:52.715 --> 00:29:53.876
Rig ht!

00:29:53.916 --> 00:29:56.908
- Promise?
- Promise!

00:30:11.200 --> 00:30:13.567
Father, Eiko, come here!
Look at this!

00:30:13.602 --> 00:30:15.570
What is it? Good heavens.

00:30:15.604 --> 00:30:18.574
Look at all the ants.
Where are they coming from?

00:30:18.607 --> 00:30:21.577
- I've never seen so many.
- I wonder why?

00:30:29.351 --> 00:30:30.477
B-29.

00:30:30.519 --> 00:30:31.748
Yeah?

00:30:33.355 --> 00:30:36.256
- Gee, and it's all alone.
- What's it doing?

00:30:38.861 --> 00:30:42.820
- Probably a spy mission.
- It's very strange.

00:30:42.865 --> 00:30:45.835
Why isn't the air raid siren
going off?

00:30:45.868 --> 00:30:47.302
I don't know.

00:31:12.261 --> 00:31:15.231
Altitude 3,600 feet.

00:31:15.264 --> 00:31:18.234
Fixed on target. Release bomb.

00:31:18.267 --> 00:31:20.463
Roger. Releasing bomb.

00:34:33.795 --> 00:34:35.263
Wow, what happened?

00:34:35.297 --> 00:34:37.197
How'd lend up here?

00:34:37.232 --> 00:34:40.202
Guess they finally decided
to bomb us.

00:34:40.235 --> 00:34:41.361
Ugh!

00:34:41.403 --> 00:34:45.863
What a mess.

00:34:47.376 --> 00:34:50.038
Hang on.

00:34:50.812 --> 00:34:52.837
She's dead!

00:34:54.316 --> 00:34:55.442
Hey!

00:34:55.484 --> 00:34:57.316
Somebody, hel...

00:35:12.367 --> 00:35:14.699
ls anybody here?

00:35:50.072 --> 00:35:51.540
Am I dreaming?

00:35:51.573 --> 00:35:53.974
Are they ghosts or what?

00:35:59.948 --> 00:36:01.382
Fire!

00:36:01.416 --> 00:36:06.513
My house is on fire!

00:36:06.555 --> 00:36:08.523
Oh, please, not my house!

00:36:08.557 --> 00:36:12.460
I'm coming. Father! Mother!
Eiko! Shinji!

00:36:15.564 --> 00:36:19.000
Hey, Shinji, where are you?

00:36:20.569 --> 00:36:23.539
Is anyone here? Where are you?

00:36:23.572 --> 00:36:24.698
Father!

00:36:24.740 --> 00:36:27.869
Please, somebody, help us!

00:36:27.909 --> 00:36:29.035
That's Mother's voice!

00:36:29.077 --> 00:36:32.138
Somebody help me! Hurry!

00:36:33.215 --> 00:36:34.546
Mother, what happened?

00:36:34.583 --> 00:36:37.052
Oh, my sweet boy, you're alive!

00:36:37.085 --> 00:36:39.053
Hurry, Mother, get us!

00:36:39.087 --> 00:36:40.384
It really hurts!

00:36:40.422 --> 00:36:43.790
Shinji! Eiko! Father!

00:36:44.926 --> 00:36:48.226
Hurry, Gen.
Help me lift this beam!

00:36:48.263 --> 00:36:49.424
Yes, Mother.

00:36:50.599 --> 00:36:54.558
Hurry up, Gen!
It's getting hotter.

00:36:54.603 --> 00:36:56.571
Hang on.

00:36:56.605 --> 00:36:58.539
Do it fast!

00:36:58.573 --> 00:37:00.541
It really hurts bad!

00:37:00.575 --> 00:37:02.543
It's so hot!

00:37:02.577 --> 00:37:04.545
Hurry, Gen! I'm scared!

00:37:04.579 --> 00:37:07.844
Hurry, Gen! I'm scared!

00:37:11.887 --> 00:37:13.582
It won't move.

00:37:13.622 --> 00:37:16.614
We'll get them out! We have to!

00:37:16.658 --> 00:37:19.059
That's enough. Go on.
Get away.

00:37:20.162 --> 00:37:21.630
What are you saying?

00:37:21.663 --> 00:37:24.132
Get out now. Go while you can!

00:37:24.166 --> 00:37:27.602
No, darling, no!
I won't! Never!

00:37:27.636 --> 00:37:29.104
Kimei.

00:37:29.137 --> 00:37:32.596
Listen to me. You've got
to go while you still can!

00:37:32.641 --> 00:37:35.110
Never! I would rather die!

00:37:35.143 --> 00:37:37.612
Kimei,
you're talking like a fool.

00:37:37.646 --> 00:37:39.136
You've got Gen and the baby
to think of now.

00:37:39.181 --> 00:37:41.377
No, I won't!

00:37:41.416 --> 00:37:44.113
I will never leave you!

00:37:44.152 --> 00:37:47.554
Gen, you know what
you have to do now, son.

00:37:47.589 --> 00:37:49.614
What do you want me to do,
Father?

00:37:49.658 --> 00:37:52.127
You get your mother
out of here now!

00:37:52.160 --> 00:37:56.119
No, Father, I won't do it!

00:37:56.164 --> 00:37:58.633
I'm scared! Gen!

00:38:02.471 --> 00:38:04.132
Oh, Mother, please, Mother...

00:38:04.172 --> 00:38:05.640
I'm so weak.

00:38:05.674 --> 00:38:08.609
Oh, why couldn't I be stronger?

00:38:08.643 --> 00:38:10.133
Gen!

00:38:10.178 --> 00:38:14.581
It's up to you to look after
your mother and the baby.

00:38:16.685 --> 00:38:19.086
They're going to need you, boy.

00:38:21.189 --> 00:38:23.556
I know you'll do your best.

00:38:30.799 --> 00:38:32.995
No, no! I won't go!

00:38:33.034 --> 00:38:37.665
I want to stay here and die!

00:38:39.274 --> 00:38:40.435
Oh, it's getting hotter!

00:38:40.475 --> 00:38:42.739
Mother, where are you?
It's really, really hot!

00:38:42.777 --> 00:38:45.246
I have to go to him!

00:38:45.280 --> 00:38:46.748
Where is everybody?

00:38:46.781 --> 00:38:49.250
Mommy!

00:38:49.284 --> 00:38:52.345
Mommy!

00:38:52.387 --> 00:38:54.981
Shinji!

00:39:05.934 --> 00:39:07.959
They're all burning up.

00:39:08.003 --> 00:39:11.803
My family...burning.

00:39:21.316 --> 00:39:24.752
They're burning like a bonfire.

00:39:24.786 --> 00:39:26.254
Are you all right, Mother?

00:39:28.523 --> 00:39:31.982
Mother,
Mother, we've got to go now.

00:39:32.027 --> 00:39:34.689
Come away from there! Hurry!

00:39:34.729 --> 00:39:37.198
Mr. Pak! Mr. Pak!

00:39:37.232 --> 00:39:38.700
Gen, is that you?

00:39:38.733 --> 00:39:41.202
Here, leave your mother to me.

00:39:41.236 --> 00:39:42.362
Hurry.

00:39:42.404 --> 00:39:43.735
Come on. Get moving.

00:40:20.575 --> 00:40:25.536
Children, grab on
to any floating pieces of wood.

00:40:25.580 --> 00:40:29.539
Keep your heads above the water.

00:40:29.584 --> 00:40:31.052
That's it. That's it.

00:40:31.086 --> 00:40:36.047
Wha--No! Hang on, children!

00:40:36.091 --> 00:40:38.492
Hang on!

00:40:40.028 --> 00:40:41.553
Well, you should be safe
here for the moment.

00:40:41.596 --> 00:40:43.564
Gen, I have to go now.

00:40:43.598 --> 00:40:46.568
Take care of your mother.
Good luck.

00:40:46.601 --> 00:40:48.091
Thanks, Mr. Pak.

00:40:49.237 --> 00:40:50.568
What's the matter, Mother?

00:40:50.605 --> 00:40:52.573
It's coming now.

00:40:52.607 --> 00:40:53.768
The baby?

00:40:53.808 --> 00:40:55.572
You must try and find
a doctor or a midwife, Gen.

00:40:55.610 --> 00:40:56.941
All right.

00:40:56.978 --> 00:41:00.073
And I'll need a basin
that will hold lots of water...

00:41:00.115 --> 00:41:02.982
and some strips of any clean
cloth you're able to find.

00:41:03.018 --> 00:41:04.486
Right.

00:41:04.519 --> 00:41:06.988
A pair of scissors and thread.

00:41:07.021 --> 00:41:09.080
What are the scissors for?

00:41:09.124 --> 00:41:13.083
Somebody will have to cut
the cord.

00:41:13.128 --> 00:41:16.098
Is there a midwife
or a doctor around anywhere?

00:41:16.131 --> 00:41:22.070
Is anyone a doctor?
I need a doctor!

00:41:22.103 --> 00:41:25.095
Listen to me!
My motherfls having a baby!

00:41:25.140 --> 00:41:27.234
Doesn't anybody know a doctor?

00:41:27.275 --> 00:41:30.245
Everything's gone crazy.
Therefls nobody to help me.

00:41:30.278 --> 00:41:32.246
What'll I do now? What'll I do?

00:41:33.648 --> 00:41:35.116
I'm sorry, Mother.

00:41:35.150 --> 00:41:39.109
I looked everywhere, but I
couldn't find anybody to help.

00:41:39.154 --> 00:41:40.280
No one.

00:41:40.322 --> 00:41:43.314
Well, we'll do it ourselves.

00:41:43.358 --> 00:41:46.328
You and me, Mother?
But that's impossible!

00:41:46.361 --> 00:41:48.830
You must try, my boy.

00:41:48.863 --> 00:41:51.332
All right, <i>l-ll</i> try.

00:41:51.366 --> 00:41:53.130
First of all, fetch some water.

00:41:53.168 --> 00:41:54.329
Got it!

00:42:01.643 --> 00:42:04.135
Be sure to have
some rags ready, Gen.

00:42:04.179 --> 00:42:07.114
You'll have to wash
the baby when it's born.

00:42:07.148 --> 00:42:09.674
Don't worry. I'm ready.

00:42:25.166 --> 00:42:29.125
You've got to be very careful
about holding up its head.

00:42:29.170 --> 00:42:31.161
Hey, this baby
doesn't look like me.

00:42:31.206 --> 00:42:35.666
It's a girl, Mother, but it
really looks like a monkey.

00:42:35.710 --> 00:42:40.147
All babies do. You did,too.

00:42:40.181 --> 00:42:43.617
Well, I guess she'll turn out
to be real pretty then.

00:42:45.086 --> 00:42:46.679
Listen here, baby.

00:42:46.721 --> 00:42:49.190
I'm the one
who brought you to life...

00:42:49.224 --> 00:42:51.693
so you better thank me
when you grow up...

00:42:51.726 --> 00:42:56.288
and you better do everything
I tell you to do, OK?

00:43:00.235 --> 00:43:02.203
They're going
to need you now, boy.

00:43:02.237 --> 00:43:04.205
It's up to you
to look after them now.

00:43:04.239 --> 00:43:06.207
It's going to be a boy!

00:43:06.241 --> 00:43:09.211
And he's going to be
my little brother!

00:43:09.244 --> 00:43:11.212
Father, are you out there?

00:43:11.246 --> 00:43:15.205
Eiko! Shinji!

00:43:15.250 --> 00:43:18.709
The baby's here, everybody!
Can you see her?

00:43:18.753 --> 00:43:20.221
It's a girl!

00:43:20.255 --> 00:43:21.848
You were wrong, Shinji.
It's a girl!

00:43:26.828 --> 00:43:31.732
Oh, why aren't you here?
Father! Shinji!

00:43:31.766 --> 00:43:34.736
She's the prettiest baby girl
in the whole world...

00:43:34.769 --> 00:43:36.737
and you never saw her.

00:43:36.771 --> 00:43:40.765
Gen, give her to me.
Let me hold her.

00:43:42.176 --> 00:43:45.237
Take a good look around,
little one.

00:43:45.280 --> 00:43:47.749
Look closely. You see?

00:43:47.782 --> 00:43:53.744
This is the war
that killed your father.

00:43:53.788 --> 00:43:56.280
Remember it.

00:44:05.800 --> 00:44:07.768
What in the world?

00:44:07.802 --> 00:44:08.792
It's raining.

00:44:10.805 --> 00:44:12.295
Stop it, stop it.

00:44:13.808 --> 00:44:15.776
What?

00:44:15.810 --> 00:44:17.505
That's not right.

00:44:17.545 --> 00:44:22.005
Mother, have you ever seen rain
that's black like this?

00:44:22.050 --> 00:44:24.781
This black rain began falling...

00:44:24.819 --> 00:44:27.789
on the northwest section
of the city.

00:44:27.822 --> 00:44:31.781
The impact
of the bomb's blast...

00:44:31.826 --> 00:44:33.794
had sent dust, debris,
and radiation...

00:44:33.828 --> 00:44:35.796
high into the atmosphere...

00:44:35.830 --> 00:44:38.800
where it gathered
in a gigantic, lethal cloud...

00:44:38.833 --> 00:44:41.803
before returning to the earth
as radioactive rain.

00:44:41.836 --> 00:44:45.033
The bomb that had
fallen on the city...

00:44:45.073 --> 00:44:48.043
detonated with a destructive
force of 20,000 tons of TNT...

00:44:48.076 --> 00:44:51.046
and generated temperatures
an excess of 4,000 degrees.

00:44:51.079 --> 00:44:54.606
Some 60% of the city
had vanished.

00:44:54.649 --> 00:44:58.017
But the damage
did not end there.

00:44:58.052 --> 00:45:00.521
The people of Hiroshima
did not know it yet...

00:45:00.555 --> 00:45:03.354
but the bomb's after-effects,
such as the black rain...

00:45:03.391 --> 00:45:05.860
would bring them
many years of suffering.

00:45:19.374 --> 00:45:22.833
Those people,
they make so much noise.

00:45:22.877 --> 00:45:25.346
How am I supposed to sleep?

00:45:25.380 --> 00:45:27.815
Perhaps if we took them
some of our water.

00:45:36.891 --> 00:45:39.553
Here.
This is some water. Drink.

00:45:44.899 --> 00:45:47.834
Go on. There's more
where this came from.

00:45:49.904 --> 00:45:52.896
Look at that woman.

00:45:53.908 --> 00:45:55.876
She's dead!

00:45:57.912 --> 00:45:59.402
I don't understand.

00:46:02.951 --> 00:46:05.420
Why? What's making them die?

00:46:05.453 --> 00:46:07.387
They died when they drank.

00:46:07.422 --> 00:46:09.914
Could something be wrong
with the water?

00:46:11.926 --> 00:46:14.395
We've got to stop them
from drinking the water.

00:46:14.429 --> 00:46:15.919
You're right.

00:46:29.310 --> 00:46:32.405
Mother, what are we going to do?

00:46:32.447 --> 00:46:34.415
Well, let me see now.

00:46:36.084 --> 00:46:38.553
We've no place to go, really.

00:46:38.586 --> 00:46:40.418
Our relatives will be dead...

00:46:40.455 --> 00:46:43.049
or if not, they'll be
no better off than we are.

00:46:43.091 --> 00:46:46.925
Frankly, son, I don't know what
we're going to do.

00:46:46.961 --> 00:46:50.920
I'm finding it difficult
to think clearly.

00:46:50.965 --> 00:46:54.060
There, there, now.
I don't have any milk.

00:46:54.102 --> 00:46:57.072
That's bad, Mother.
Babies need milk to live.

00:46:57.105 --> 00:47:00.939
We've eaten nothing for 3 days,
and my milk has dried up.

00:47:00.975 --> 00:47:03.103
When mothers go hungry,
their babies go hungry, too.

00:47:03.144 --> 00:47:08.446
I really must try to find
some food, for her sake.

00:47:08.483 --> 00:47:11.612
You just leave everything to me.

00:47:11.652 --> 00:47:13.620
What do you mean?
What can you do?

00:47:13.655 --> 00:47:16.647
It's up to me
to see we have food.

00:47:20.661 --> 00:47:23.460
Father said it's up to me now.

00:47:23.498 --> 00:47:26.468
I won't ever let you die.
You won't have to worry.

00:47:26.501 --> 00:47:28.663
I'll protect you!

00:47:30.805 --> 00:47:32.637
But where am I going
to find food around here?

00:47:32.674 --> 00:47:35.109
Hey,
where did you get that rice?

00:47:35.143 --> 00:47:37.134
My mom and baby sister
are hungry.

00:47:37.178 --> 00:47:39.146
There's army trucks
distributing food.

00:47:39.180 --> 00:47:41.148
You haven't seen them?

00:47:41.182 --> 00:47:43.651
Oh, that's great.
Where are they?

00:47:43.684 --> 00:47:45.982
Ah, forget it!
Find 'em yourself!

00:47:46.020 --> 00:47:48.648
I got this rice
down by the bridge.

00:47:48.690 --> 00:47:50.158
By the bridge?
I know where that is.

00:47:50.191 --> 00:47:52.523
An army truck, right?

00:47:56.030 --> 00:47:59.864
Wait!
Do you have any more rice?

00:48:10.278 --> 00:48:12.007
Dead bodies. Nothing else.

00:48:12.046 --> 00:48:13.514
Get that fire started.

00:48:13.548 --> 00:48:16.210
We've got to burn them
before they rot.

00:48:22.757 --> 00:48:25.021
My God.
Therefls just so many of them.

00:48:25.059 --> 00:48:26.720
When will it stop?

00:48:26.761 --> 00:48:28.525
The smell's awful.

00:48:28.563 --> 00:48:31.260
There must be more dead people
here than live ones.

00:48:42.844 --> 00:48:45.575
Hey, look at this--
a fireman's hat.

00:48:56.557 --> 00:49:00.084
Those soldiers are so mean.

00:49:02.563 --> 00:49:05.965
They're just treating
those people like bags of trash.

00:49:08.102 --> 00:49:14.064
It's almost like
they never lived at all.

00:49:14.108 --> 00:49:17.510
Maybe this is what hell's like.

00:49:30.091 --> 00:49:32.082
Look at all these damn maggots.

00:49:32.126 --> 00:49:35.562
I didn't even notice them.

00:49:35.596 --> 00:49:38.088
When they start
moving around in there...

00:49:38.132 --> 00:49:39.566
it itches like crazy.

00:49:39.600 --> 00:49:41.591
Do you think it's all right
to eat them?

00:49:41.636 --> 00:49:44.105
Are you crazy? It's not time
to talk about food.

00:49:44.138 --> 00:49:47.073
Please, can somebody help me?

00:49:47.108 --> 00:49:51.102
Is there anyone here
who can help feed my baby?

00:49:51.145 --> 00:49:54.171
She needs milk. She's starving.

00:49:57.652 --> 00:49:59.643
Oh, please, will you--

00:50:09.163 --> 00:50:12.622
Please, isn't there anybody who
can help me with a little milk?

00:50:12.667 --> 00:50:14.135
My baby is starving.

00:50:14.168 --> 00:50:17.570
Be quiet! Let it die!
It's better off!

00:50:17.605 --> 00:50:20.074
Kill it! Kill it!

00:50:20.108 --> 00:50:22.008
You're mad to say that!

00:50:22.043 --> 00:50:24.740
All right, then.
I will kill it for you!

00:50:24.779 --> 00:50:27.646
Give it to me! Give it to me!

00:50:27.682 --> 00:50:30.208
No! Please! Not my baby!

00:50:38.192 --> 00:50:39.591
There, little one.

00:50:41.162 --> 00:50:45.121
Eat now. Take all I have.

00:50:45.166 --> 00:50:46.964
You still have milk.

00:50:47.001 --> 00:50:50.164
I can't believe I really
said those terrible things.

00:50:50.204 --> 00:50:53.174
It's just that your baby
reminded me of my own.

00:50:53.207 --> 00:50:55.471
She's dead now, over there.

00:50:55.509 --> 00:50:58.444
I have no one to drink my milk.

00:50:58.479 --> 00:51:02.677
Your baby's welcome
to have all I have left.

00:51:02.717 --> 00:51:04.207
Thank you.

00:51:05.219 --> 00:51:07.187
You're lucky, my child.

00:51:07.221 --> 00:51:09.349
So very lucky.

00:51:10.391 --> 00:51:15.227
Everybody's dead.
Everything8 gone.

00:51:18.733 --> 00:51:21.202
How come you're shivering
when it's so hot?

00:51:21.235 --> 00:51:23.203
Do you feel sick or something?

00:51:23.237 --> 00:51:27.196
I'm freezing. Musfve caught
a chill from the rain.

00:51:27.241 --> 00:51:29.209
Hey, I think you wet your pants.

00:51:29.243 --> 00:51:32.406
Shut up, you brat!
What are you talking about?

00:51:33.748 --> 00:51:35.307
Blood!

00:51:35.349 --> 00:51:38.216
Musfve sat in something.

00:51:38.252 --> 00:51:40.721
Hey, somebody
cut holes in your hair!

00:51:40.755 --> 00:51:43.554
Listen, kid, I'll cut holes
in you, if you don't--

00:51:45.760 --> 00:51:47.751
<i>'My God. What's happening?</i>

00:51:52.633 --> 00:51:57.730
Mister, what's wrong?
Do you need some help?

00:51:57.772 --> 00:51:58.762
What's wrong? Hey!

00:52:01.642 --> 00:52:03.235
Help!

00:52:05.780 --> 00:52:08.215
I need help!

00:52:09.283 --> 00:52:11.251
Get up!

00:52:11.285 --> 00:52:13.276
I've got you.

00:52:14.789 --> 00:52:16.279
Come on, "P!

00:52:18.793 --> 00:52:22.730
You know, I don't think
it's going to work.

00:52:29.737 --> 00:52:35.699
There! That's a pretty clever
stretcher, huh?

00:52:35.743 --> 00:52:38.610
Hang in there, soldier.
You'll be fine.

00:52:39.714 --> 00:52:44.811
Hello! Does anybody know
where the hospital is?

00:52:56.263 --> 00:52:57.788
Please help me.

00:52:57.832 --> 00:53:01.291
Tend only to those who
show some chance of recovery.

00:53:01.335 --> 00:53:02.803
Yes, sir.

00:53:02.837 --> 00:53:04.805
We don't have
enough medicine for them...

00:53:04.839 --> 00:53:06.830
let alone all these others.

00:53:08.342 --> 00:53:10.743
Hey, somebody should
look at this soldier.

00:53:10.778 --> 00:53:12.803
He's real bad, I think.

00:53:12.847 --> 00:53:14.315
Another one.

00:53:14.348 --> 00:53:17.807
Tell me, boy,
was he vomiting blood...

00:53:17.852 --> 00:53:20.253
and complaining
that he was cold?

00:53:20.287 --> 00:53:23.746
Right. I guess that means you
know what's wrong with him.

00:53:23.791 --> 00:53:26.260
No use looking at this one.

00:53:26.293 --> 00:53:28.387
This soldier's dead.

00:53:28.429 --> 00:53:29.828
God help us.

00:53:29.864 --> 00:53:32.390
Is it possible that one bomb
could have done all this?

00:53:32.433 --> 00:53:34.834
The initial explosion
of the atomic bomb...

00:53:34.869 --> 00:53:36.769
claimed more than 100,000 lives.

00:53:36.804 --> 00:53:38.829
But that was only the beginning.

00:53:38.873 --> 00:53:40.341
The radiation remained...

00:53:40.374 --> 00:53:42.843
contaminating soldiers
cleaning up the city...

00:53:42.877 --> 00:53:45.346
as well as those relatives
of the victims...

00:53:45.379 --> 00:53:46.778
who came looking for them.

00:53:46.814 --> 00:53:48.339
For years afterwards...

00:53:48.382 --> 00:53:52.341
these people would suffer
from leukemia and cancer--

00:53:52.386 --> 00:53:56.880
part of the collateral damage
inflicted by the bomb.

00:54:30.858 --> 00:54:32.917
God help us.

00:54:34.428 --> 00:54:38.422
Is it possible that one bomb
could have done all this?

00:54:39.867 --> 00:54:43.929
Damn it! Damn it!

00:54:46.440 --> 00:54:47.805
Huh? What's this?

00:54:49.443 --> 00:54:52.344
Rice!
But it looks like charcoal.

00:54:52.380 --> 00:54:55.441
This must've been
some kind of storehouse.

00:54:56.951 --> 00:55:00.410
What a waste! All this rice
for people to eat...

00:55:00.454 --> 00:55:03.446
and it's been burnt
to a crisp! Damn it!

00:55:20.975 --> 00:55:24.104
Underneath, it's OK!

00:55:24.144 --> 00:55:25.942
I found a gold mine!

00:55:25.980 --> 00:55:29.541
Ha! There's more rice
than we'll be able to eat!

00:55:31.485 --> 00:55:33.476
Ha ha! Hooray!

00:55:36.323 --> 00:55:38.951
Found some pickles, too.

00:55:38.992 --> 00:55:42.451
Mother, you and the baby will
never have to be hungry again!

00:55:42.496 --> 00:55:45.466
Gen, you've done well.
Thank you.

00:55:45.499 --> 00:55:48.958
Well, I see
you got the camp all set up.

00:55:49.003 --> 00:55:50.471
She's sleeping, huh?

00:55:50.504 --> 00:55:53.474
Hey, isn't it time we came up
with a name for her?

00:55:53.507 --> 00:55:57.000
I think you're right.
Our daughter should have a name.

00:55:58.512 --> 00:56:00.981
There are more and more
fires all the time.

00:56:01.015 --> 00:56:02.483
They're burning the dead.

00:56:02.516 --> 00:56:04.484
There are so many dead, Mother.

00:56:04.518 --> 00:56:06.987
- So many.
- It's horrible.

00:56:07.021 --> 00:56:09.012
Yes, it is, Gen.

00:56:11.592 --> 00:56:13.993
- Mother.
- What?

00:56:14.028 --> 00:56:17.487
I hope she always has
lots of friends.

00:56:17.531 --> 00:56:20.557
I know what--
let's call her Tomoko.

00:56:20.601 --> 00:56:24.231
Yes. That means friend.
Very good.

00:56:24.271 --> 00:56:27.002
Well, OK. It's all set, then.
You're Tomoko.

00:56:27.040 --> 00:56:29.008
Gen, what's happened
to your hair?

00:56:29.043 --> 00:56:30.511
Those bald spots.

00:56:30.544 --> 00:56:32.569
What are you talking about?

00:56:32.613 --> 00:56:35.583
MY hair!

00:56:35.616 --> 00:56:37.050
MY hair!

00:56:47.061 --> 00:56:50.520
This soldier's dead.
God help us.

00:56:50.564 --> 00:56:53.363
Is it possible that one bomb
could have done all this?

00:56:53.400 --> 00:56:54.526
Gen!

00:56:54.568 --> 00:56:57.538
Don't let it happen to me,
Mother!

00:56:57.571 --> 00:57:00.040
I don't want to die!

00:57:00.074 --> 00:57:01.542
There, there, my little one.

00:57:01.575 --> 00:57:03.543
You're not going to die,
do you hear?

00:57:03.577 --> 00:57:05.671
You are not going to die.

00:57:05.712 --> 00:57:07.544
After the bombing
of Hiroshima...

00:57:07.581 --> 00:57:11.040
the United States
issued an ultimatum...

00:57:11.085 --> 00:57:13.053
calling on Japan to surrender...

00:57:13.087 --> 00:57:16.546
and threatening to drop a second
atomic bomb if it did not.

00:57:16.590 --> 00:57:19.560
The Japanese high command
ignored the warning.

00:57:19.593 --> 00:57:25.054
They made certain the extent
of the damage to Hiroshima...

00:57:25.099 --> 00:57:29.661
was little reported.

00:57:29.703 --> 00:57:31.137
Three days later
on August 9th...

00:57:31.171 --> 00:57:33.105
another B-29 appeared
in the sky above Nagasaki.

00:57:56.330 --> 00:57:59.163
Japan's high command
was convinced at last.

00:57:59.199 --> 00:58:01.293
On August 15th,
the emperor Hirohito...

00:58:01.335 --> 00:58:03.804
in the first public address
made by a Japanese sovereign...

00:58:03.837 --> 00:58:06.306
announced
that the war was over.

00:59:01.328 --> 00:59:03.319
Yes, Mother?

00:59:03.363 --> 00:59:05.331
Your father, sister,
and brother...

00:59:05.365 --> 00:59:08.335
they've all been taken away
from us, haven't they?

00:59:08.368 --> 00:59:11.338
That's right.
All of them are dead, Mother.

00:59:17.878 --> 00:59:20.848
What's the matter, mister?
Why are you crying?

00:59:20.881 --> 00:59:24.340
The emperor announced it
on the radio just now.

00:59:24.384 --> 00:59:27.354
Japan has been defeated.

00:59:27.388 --> 00:59:31.347
We've lost the war.
We've surrendered.

00:59:31.391 --> 00:59:34.725
Tell me, why now?
Why not before?

00:59:40.400 --> 00:59:42.869
It's all right.
Come on, Mother, cheer up.

00:59:42.903 --> 00:59:45.873
We're going to be OK. Trust me.

00:59:45.906 --> 00:59:48.876
I've already started planning
what to do.

00:59:48.909 --> 00:59:53.369
And I know the first thing
we're going to need--a house.

00:59:53.413 --> 00:59:57.372
August 15,1945.

00:59:57.417 --> 01:00:01.752
Japan officially surrenders
to the Allied powers.

01:00:04.925 --> 01:00:07.895
Don't cry, Tomoko.
Hush now, hush.

01:00:07.928 --> 01:00:10.898
I still don't have
enough milk for her.

01:00:10.931 --> 01:00:12.899
We'll have to find some for her.

01:00:12.933 --> 01:00:14.901
She needs milk,
not this rice soup.

01:00:14.935 --> 01:00:16.903
I never thought it possible...

01:00:16.937 --> 01:00:20.896
but we're running out
of rice, too.

01:00:20.941 --> 01:00:23.933
Come and eat now.
Hand her to me.

01:00:25.946 --> 01:00:28.415
If I could only find some kind
of work, but it's hopeless.

01:00:28.448 --> 01:00:30.382
We're in quite a fix.

01:00:30.417 --> 01:00:34.945
Don't worry.
I'll think of something.

01:00:36.456 --> 01:00:38.424
What are you doing?

01:00:38.458 --> 01:00:40.426
Who are you?

01:00:40.461 --> 01:00:41.690
Hey!

01:00:43.464 --> 01:00:45.933
Come here, you little thief!

01:00:45.966 --> 01:00:47.127
Gotcha!

01:00:50.971 --> 01:00:54.930
If I weren't so hungry,
I'd beat you to a pulp.

01:00:54.975 --> 01:00:57.967
So what? Don't you think
we're hungry, too?

01:00:58.979 --> 01:01:00.344
Huh?

01:01:00.380 --> 01:01:03.839
Mother, look at this boy.

01:01:03.884 --> 01:01:05.943
Look at his face.
Show her your face.

01:01:05.986 --> 01:01:07.317
What are you doing?

01:01:11.892 --> 01:01:14.452
Whoever Shinji is, I'm not him.

01:01:14.494 --> 01:01:15.928
I thought you were
my little brother.

01:01:15.962 --> 01:01:17.088
I'm not!

01:01:17.130 --> 01:01:20.100
No, of course you aren't.
He's dead.

01:01:20.133 --> 01:01:22.966
My name is Ryuta Kondo.

01:01:23.003 --> 01:01:25.904
I haven't eaten all week.

01:01:25.939 --> 01:01:29.398
Then I smelled your rice.
I couldn't help it.

01:01:29.443 --> 01:01:31.468
Where's your family, Ryuta?

01:01:31.512 --> 01:01:33.981
They were all killed
in the explosion.

01:01:34.014 --> 01:01:37.473
You look exactly like
my little brother Shinji.

01:01:37.518 --> 01:01:39.418
Well, I'm not. I'm Ryuta!

01:01:41.288 --> 01:01:42.881
Here. You can have my rice,
if you want it.

01:01:42.923 --> 01:01:45.392
You'd give it to me?

01:01:45.425 --> 01:01:46.551
Take it.

01:01:46.593 --> 01:01:49.221
You mean I can have all of it?

01:01:49.262 --> 01:01:50.423
Sure.

01:01:53.433 --> 01:01:55.401
Slow down.
You'll make yourself sick.

01:01:55.436 --> 01:01:57.905
No.
You might want it back again.

01:01:57.938 --> 01:01:59.406
I won't want it back. Really.

01:01:59.439 --> 01:02:01.498
Why should I believe you?

01:02:01.541 --> 01:02:03.669
Will you relax?

01:02:03.710 --> 01:02:06.179
Where have you lived
since the bomb fell, my boy?

01:02:06.213 --> 01:02:09.148
Out in the open.

01:02:09.182 --> 01:02:11.708
If you're still hungry,
you're welcome to finish mine.

01:02:12.719 --> 01:02:13.845
Sit down.

01:02:13.887 --> 01:02:15.685
You really mean it?

01:02:20.460 --> 01:02:23.919
Mother, he even behaves
like Shinji. It's amazing.

01:02:23.964 --> 01:02:26.433
It is remarkable, Gen.

01:02:26.466 --> 01:02:31.028
I've heard it said everyone has
five doubles of him or herself.

01:02:31.071 --> 01:02:34.564
Still, that he should have
found us, it's uncanny.

01:02:34.608 --> 01:02:36.576
Hmm, is there any more?

01:02:36.610 --> 01:02:38.203
There's nothing in there.

01:02:40.614 --> 01:02:43.606
Somehow it seems
like he belongs here.

01:02:43.650 --> 01:02:46.176
I know what you mean.

01:02:46.220 --> 01:02:47.585
Are you thinking
what I'm thinking?

01:02:47.621 --> 01:02:50.420
Well, you know we're having
a difficult enough time...

01:02:50.457 --> 01:02:52.653
making ends meet as it is...

01:02:52.692 --> 01:02:54.922
but still,
if Shinji were alive--

01:02:54.962 --> 01:02:56.930
So, it's all right then?

01:03:01.935 --> 01:03:04.063
Wow, that was the best!

01:03:04.104 --> 01:03:07.597
I almost don't even feel hungry.

01:03:07.641 --> 01:03:10.770
We've been thinking. Would you
like to have a home again?

01:03:10.811 --> 01:03:12.609
Yeah, you want to stay here?

01:03:12.646 --> 01:03:15.115
And live with us?

01:03:15.148 --> 01:03:17.515
Be part of our family?

01:03:17.551 --> 01:03:18.916
Stay and live with you?

01:03:20.921 --> 01:03:24.016
I won't be much help.

01:03:24.057 --> 01:03:26.583
I'm only a kid,
but I can give you a back rub.

01:03:26.627 --> 01:03:28.652
Daddy always said
I was a good back rubber.

01:03:28.695 --> 01:03:30.891
That's very kind of you,
but you don't have to.

01:03:30.931 --> 01:03:33.901
We're not asking for anything
in return, child.

01:03:33.934 --> 01:03:35.925
You'll just be
one of the family.

01:03:35.969 --> 01:03:38.597
Really? Gee, thanks.

01:03:38.638 --> 01:03:40.470
L---

01:03:43.443 --> 01:03:45.605
OK, stop it. Stop crying.

01:03:45.646 --> 01:03:48.616
You're going to wake up
Tomoko if you--

01:03:48.648 --> 01:03:50.446
Now we've got two of them
howling.

01:03:50.484 --> 01:03:52.612
That's all right.
You go right on and cry.

01:03:52.653 --> 01:03:53.950
I don't worry about her.

01:03:53.987 --> 01:03:55.546
Your baby looks funny.
Is it sick?

01:03:55.589 --> 01:03:58.024
Yeah. Malnutrition.

01:03:58.058 --> 01:03:59.423
That means she's not
getting enough to eat.

01:03:59.459 --> 01:04:02.622
She needs milk.

01:04:02.663 --> 01:04:05.792
Hey, I've got an idea.

01:04:07.033 --> 01:04:09.001
Hey, will anyone give us a job?

01:04:09.036 --> 01:04:11.061
Anybody got a job for us?
Any job at all?

01:04:11.104 --> 01:04:12.230
Anybody?

01:04:12.272 --> 01:04:13.398
Hello!

01:04:13.440 --> 01:04:15.909
Any job at all!

01:04:15.943 --> 01:04:18.344
Nobody looks very interested,
do they?

01:04:18.378 --> 01:04:20.346
No, big brother.

01:04:20.380 --> 01:04:22.906
Wait a minute.
What did you call me, Ryuta?

01:04:22.949 --> 01:04:24.917
Big brother.
What's wrong with that?

01:04:24.951 --> 01:04:26.282
Nothing! Say it again.

01:04:26.319 --> 01:04:27.445
Big brother.

01:04:27.487 --> 01:04:28.648
Again!

01:04:28.688 --> 01:04:32.556
Big brother. Why?
Do you like being called that?

01:04:32.592 --> 01:04:34.959
A lot!

01:04:34.995 --> 01:04:37.430
You want me to say it
some more then?

01:04:37.464 --> 01:04:39.193
Big brother!

01:04:39.232 --> 01:04:41.223
My big brother Gen!

01:04:41.268 --> 01:04:44.670
Hey, listen, everybody.
This is my big brother!

01:04:44.704 --> 01:04:45.899
Idiot!

01:04:45.939 --> 01:04:48.670
You boys, did you mean it...

01:04:48.708 --> 01:04:49.971
when you said you'd take
any kind of job?

01:04:50.010 --> 01:04:51.944
Yep. You've got something?

01:04:51.978 --> 01:04:54.640
Yes, I believe I have...

01:04:54.681 --> 01:04:55.944
if you boys would like to
make 10 yen a day.

01:04:55.982 --> 01:04:57.814
Ten yen? You bet, mister!

01:04:57.851 --> 01:04:59.683
Ten yen?
Yeah, of course we would.

01:04:59.720 --> 01:05:02.121
Well, then, come with me.

01:05:03.490 --> 01:05:06.949
- Is this your house?
- You must be a millionaire.

01:05:06.994 --> 01:05:08.826
Hush, keep your voices down.

01:05:10.397 --> 01:05:13.230
Daddy's found two more boys.

01:05:13.266 --> 01:05:14.825
They'll run away,
just like the others.

01:05:14.868 --> 01:05:17.997
This is where you will work.

01:05:18.038 --> 01:05:20.063
Peuw!

01:05:20.106 --> 01:05:22.097
It really stinks.

01:05:22.142 --> 01:05:23.610
What's in here?

01:05:23.644 --> 01:05:25.009
Smells like an outhouse!

01:05:25.045 --> 01:05:29.004
It's full of worms and flies.
Is that guy dead?

01:05:29.049 --> 01:05:30.346
Yecch!

01:05:30.383 --> 01:05:33.683
Seiji, I've found two more boys
to look after you.

01:05:33.720 --> 01:05:36.382
Ask them to do anything.
They're being paid well enough.

01:05:36.423 --> 01:05:39.688
- Wait, Eizo.
- Look after him well.

01:05:39.726 --> 01:05:40.852
Come back!

01:05:40.894 --> 01:05:42.862
Can't we talk for a while?

01:05:42.896 --> 01:05:44.386
Brother!

01:05:49.636 --> 01:05:51.866
I knew they'd do that.

01:05:51.905 --> 01:05:53.395
They'll be gone in no time.

01:05:53.440 --> 01:05:56.375
They stuck him in there
until he dies, I guess.

01:05:56.409 --> 01:05:59.037
Disgusting.
What should we do about him?

01:05:59.079 --> 01:06:01.377
Ten yen will buy a lot of milk.

01:06:01.415 --> 01:06:02.541
Sure will.

01:06:02.582 --> 01:06:03.708
Hey, you buzzards!

01:06:03.750 --> 01:06:05.878
- Does he mean us?
- Looks that way.

01:06:05.919 --> 01:06:09.321
Get these maggots off me
and clean up around here. Now!

01:06:09.356 --> 01:06:10.915
Yes, sir!

01:06:10.957 --> 01:06:12.391
Whatever you say!

01:06:12.425 --> 01:06:14.052
The worms crawl in,
the worms crawl out...

01:06:14.094 --> 01:06:15.562
The worms play pinochle
on your snout...

01:06:15.595 --> 01:06:17.063
And when you see
the hearse go by...

01:06:17.097 --> 01:06:20.397
You'll know that you're
the next to die.

01:06:20.434 --> 01:06:22.732
They usually run off by now.

01:06:22.769 --> 01:06:24.203
Those boys are crazy.

01:06:24.237 --> 01:06:27.571
Girls, I've told you
to stay away from your uncle.

01:06:27.607 --> 01:06:29.905
Do you want to be infected?

01:06:29.943 --> 01:06:32.571
My dear,
I'm tired of his being here.

01:06:32.612 --> 01:06:34.410
Seiji should be in a hospital.

01:06:34.447 --> 01:06:38.145
The hospitals are overflowing
with bomb victims like him.

01:06:38.185 --> 01:06:39.619
Don't be silly.

01:06:39.653 --> 01:06:41.143
With your money,
he'd have the best of care.

01:06:41.187 --> 01:06:44.589
You must try not to resent
his presence in our home.

01:06:44.624 --> 01:06:47.116
He's my brother and therefore
my responsibility.

01:06:47.160 --> 01:06:49.356
Oh, you are such a hypocrite.

01:06:49.396 --> 01:06:51.194
You know you loathe going
near him as much as I do...

01:06:51.231 --> 01:06:53.598
and it's no wonder.

01:06:53.633 --> 01:06:54.998
He stinks. He looks ghastly.

01:06:55.035 --> 01:06:56.901
He's always roaring
and shouting like a savage.

01:06:56.937 --> 01:06:59.031
The neighbors act like
we live in a haunted house.

01:06:59.072 --> 01:07:01.666
At least think of the girls,
if nothing else.

01:07:01.708 --> 01:07:04.939
It will be a blessing
for all of us if he dies soon.

01:07:07.447 --> 01:07:08.846
Little idiot!

01:07:10.550 --> 01:07:12.348
What was that all about?

01:07:12.385 --> 01:07:15.150
Were you trying
to tear my skin off?

01:07:15.188 --> 01:07:16.622
I try to be careful...

01:07:16.656 --> 01:07:18.852
but those maggots keep getting
stuck in the scabs like glue.

01:07:18.892 --> 01:07:20.291
I don't want to hear it!

01:07:20.327 --> 01:07:24.286
You have to be more careful,
you little buzzard.

01:07:24.330 --> 01:07:25.820
Listen here--

01:07:25.865 --> 01:07:27.765
You think anyone will stop me
if I wring his neck?

01:07:27.801 --> 01:07:28.962
Wait. Calm down.

01:07:29.002 --> 01:07:32.461
Fetch me that gray book
on the desk, buzzard.

01:07:32.505 --> 01:07:34.564
Stop calling me that.

01:07:34.607 --> 01:07:35.972
My namefls Gen.
I'm not a buzzard!

01:07:36.009 --> 01:07:38.444
That's right! Me, neither.
And my name's Ryuta Kondo.

01:07:38.478 --> 01:07:41.641
You're nothing but scavengers
living off my rotting flesh.

01:07:41.681 --> 01:07:43.149
Buzzards, all of you!

01:07:43.183 --> 01:07:44.981
You're no different
from the others.

01:07:46.019 --> 01:07:48.249
Wait! Don't forget the 10 yen!

01:07:48.288 --> 01:07:50.484
Right! Allow me!

01:07:50.524 --> 01:07:52.151
Here.

01:07:55.028 --> 01:07:58.089
Now go get it.

01:07:58.131 --> 01:08:00.862
Oh, my, you dropped it.

01:08:00.900 --> 01:08:03.835
Bring me some water over here.
I'm thirsty.

01:08:03.870 --> 01:08:06.567
Here's your book.

01:08:06.606 --> 01:08:08.267
Pick it up.

01:08:08.308 --> 01:08:09.434
Leave it there!

01:08:09.476 --> 01:08:11.171
We'll never get our 10 yen now.

01:08:11.211 --> 01:08:13.680
Oh, forget about the 10 yen.

01:08:13.713 --> 01:08:15.977
It's nowhere near enough!

01:08:16.015 --> 01:08:18.074
Take that!

01:08:18.118 --> 01:08:20.143
And that!

01:08:21.288 --> 01:08:24.383
You're just a spoiled brat,
even if you are a grownup.

01:08:24.424 --> 01:08:27.860
Now I know why they stuck you
out here all by yourself.

01:08:27.894 --> 01:08:29.191
We're leaving!

01:08:29.229 --> 01:08:30.924
Yeah. We quit!

01:08:30.964 --> 01:08:33.262
Wait. Don't go!
Gen, Ryuta--

01:08:33.299 --> 01:08:37.258
Calling us by our names
is not going to help.

01:08:37.304 --> 01:08:38.794
It's too late.

01:08:40.807 --> 01:08:43.276
I'm sorry I hit you.

01:08:43.310 --> 01:08:45.779
No, no. I'm glad that you did.

01:08:45.812 --> 01:08:48.747
Come on!
You like being slapped around?

01:08:48.782 --> 01:08:50.944
That's kind of weird.

01:08:50.984 --> 01:08:52.577
You want to hit him this time?

01:08:52.619 --> 01:08:53.780
My pleasure.

01:08:53.820 --> 01:08:57.256
That's right, that's right.
Hit me. I won't mind.

01:08:57.290 --> 01:09:00.316
Wait a minute. It's
not normal to want to be hit.

01:09:00.360 --> 01:09:03.728
When you've gone without human
contact as long as I have...

01:09:03.763 --> 01:09:06.528
you're grateful
for anything, even a slap.

01:09:06.566 --> 01:09:08.557
Funny how people change.

01:09:08.601 --> 01:09:11.127
My brother and his family
used to be fond of me...

01:09:11.171 --> 01:09:13.230
before the bomb did this to me.

01:09:13.273 --> 01:09:16.538
Now they've all left me
out here to die.

01:09:16.576 --> 01:09:18.237
My only visitors...

01:09:18.278 --> 01:09:20.747
are the people my brother
has paid to look after me...

01:09:20.780 --> 01:09:23.750
and none of them has ever
lasted very long.

01:09:23.783 --> 01:09:27.242
You were the only ones that
treat me as something more...

01:09:27.287 --> 01:09:28.755
than a freak or a corpse.

01:09:28.788 --> 01:09:31.883
You treated me like
a human being, and I'm grateful.

01:09:38.198 --> 01:09:41.031
- Ryuta.
- Yeah, big brother?

01:09:41.067 --> 01:09:43.468
- You go tell Mother where I am.
- And you?

01:09:43.503 --> 01:09:45.835
I'll stay here for a while, OK?

01:09:45.872 --> 01:09:48.136
I understand.
I'll tell her. Bye!

01:09:50.577 --> 01:09:53.274
I'm here. Don't worry.
I'm not going to run off.

01:09:53.313 --> 01:09:55.281
Thanks.

01:09:55.315 --> 01:09:56.476
Stop that.

01:09:56.516 --> 01:09:59.144
Come on, Seiji, no more crying.

01:09:59.185 --> 01:10:01.620
The only way
you'll ever get better...

01:10:01.655 --> 01:10:04.249
is to laugh a little,
like this.

01:10:04.290 --> 01:10:06.281
Like what?

01:10:06.326 --> 01:10:08.124
Don't do that!

01:10:08.161 --> 01:10:10.061
This!

01:10:15.235 --> 01:10:19.229
The boy's right.
I can't just give up.

01:10:19.272 --> 01:10:22.799
I never thought
I'd be able to paint again...

01:10:22.843 --> 01:10:26.245
but I won't know if I don't try.

01:10:38.592 --> 01:10:40.890
It's no use! I can't!

01:10:40.927 --> 01:10:42.861
Sure you can. You can do it!

01:10:42.896 --> 01:10:45.831
Yeah, keep trying.
Don't give up now!

01:10:45.865 --> 01:10:49.529
All right, <i>l-ll</i> try.

01:11:01.648 --> 01:11:04.015
There's 100 yen for you.

01:11:04.050 --> 01:11:05.848
One hundred?

01:11:05.885 --> 01:11:07.751
Zowie!

01:11:07.787 --> 01:11:10.347
I might almost say
that it's a miracle...

01:11:10.390 --> 01:11:12.859
what you
have done for my brother.

01:11:12.892 --> 01:11:15.452
I'm very grateful to you
for making him happy again.

01:11:15.495 --> 01:11:17.896
Seriously?
My brother said that?

01:11:17.931 --> 01:11:20.730
Uh-huh,
and he gave us enough money...

01:11:20.767 --> 01:11:22.963
to buy all the milk
we'll ever need.

01:11:23.003 --> 01:11:25.973
You deserve it.
You two will come again?

01:11:26.006 --> 01:11:28.236
Sure,
we'll come to check up on you.

01:11:28.274 --> 01:11:29.469
Remember, never give up!

01:11:29.509 --> 01:11:32.376
Don't worry, you have my word.
I never will.

01:11:32.412 --> 01:11:34.437
You two have shown me
that nothing is impossible!

01:11:34.481 --> 01:11:36.916
Oh, we like sweet potatoes...

01:11:36.950 --> 01:11:39.009
We like 'em a lot...

01:11:39.052 --> 01:11:41.783
We like 'em baked
all soft and hot...

01:11:41.821 --> 01:11:43.880
We eat so many
that our tummies get big...

01:11:43.923 --> 01:11:49.157
And we fart, fart, fart,
like a couple of pigs...

01:11:49.195 --> 01:11:52.893
What do we do like
a couple of pigs?

01:11:52.933 --> 01:11:54.628
Fish here! Fresh fish!

01:11:56.736 --> 01:11:58.932
One at a time!

01:12:01.441 --> 01:12:04.069
All right, who wants some?

01:12:04.110 --> 01:12:05.544
Milk, ladies and gentlemen!

01:12:05.578 --> 01:12:08.411
I've got it,
and it's yours for a price.

01:12:08.448 --> 01:12:10.416
Who wants milk?

01:12:10.450 --> 01:12:11.918
Powdered milk!
Better than fresh!

01:12:11.952 --> 01:12:13.420
Really. Straight from America.

01:12:13.453 --> 01:12:16.650
Well, don't be shy.
Anyone want some?

01:12:16.689 --> 01:12:20.421
Excuse me.
I'll take some of that milk.

01:12:20.460 --> 01:12:23.862
Yeah? You got any money on you,
little boy?

01:12:23.897 --> 01:12:25.490
Sure, I've got money.

01:12:25.532 --> 01:12:26.863
See?

01:12:26.900 --> 01:12:29.335
The kid's got the cash,
all right.

01:12:29.369 --> 01:12:33.431
Tomoko, I hope you're hungry,
'cause we're coming...

01:12:33.473 --> 01:12:37.842
with lots and lots of milk!

01:12:37.877 --> 01:12:39.174
We got the milk!

01:12:41.981 --> 01:12:43.415
Lots of it!

01:12:43.449 --> 01:12:45.781
The milk patrol to the rescue!

01:13:02.502 --> 01:13:04.163
Mother!

01:13:04.204 --> 01:13:05.672
Hello!

01:13:06.973 --> 01:13:09.340
Look! You'll never guess
what we've got.

01:13:10.376 --> 01:13:12.743
Milk! So much milk!

01:13:12.779 --> 01:13:14.247
We bought it in the market.

01:13:14.280 --> 01:13:17.215
It's in cans from America.
It's better than fresh.

01:13:17.250 --> 01:13:18.911
Yeah, just look at all of it.

01:13:18.952 --> 01:13:22.320
Tomoko should be so glad.

01:13:22.355 --> 01:13:26.019
Mission accomplished, Captain.

01:13:26.059 --> 01:13:27.083
Good work, soldier.

01:13:27.127 --> 01:13:28.526
Banzafl

01:13:30.497 --> 01:13:32.989
Company eyes left!

01:13:33.032 --> 01:13:35.091
Look, Mother,
all the milk you'll ever...

01:13:57.256 --> 01:14:03.127
Dear boys, too late.
Too late!

01:14:17.577 --> 01:14:21.377
<i>'Tameka, open your eyes..</i>

01:14:21.414 --> 01:14:23.473
No, you can't die!

01:14:23.516 --> 01:14:25.348
You can't die, little sister.

01:14:25.385 --> 01:14:27.285
No! We've got
all this milk for you.

01:14:27.320 --> 01:14:29.448
Couldn't you wait
just a little longer?

01:14:42.535 --> 01:14:45.061
Don't go, little sister.

01:14:45.104 --> 01:14:46.697
Don! go!

01:14:49.008 --> 01:14:51.375
How can you leave
without saying good-bye?

01:14:54.047 --> 01:14:56.573
It's not fair!

01:14:56.616 --> 01:14:58.277
I did everything I could!

01:14:58.318 --> 01:15:03.085
Why couldn't she have waited?

01:15:14.100 --> 01:15:22.100
Father, Eiko, Shinji,
I couldn't save Tomoko.

01:15:22.241 --> 01:15:24.266
I'm sorry.

01:16:14.360 --> 01:16:16.522
You know,
I heard this man saying...

01:16:16.562 --> 01:16:20.157
the grass won't grow here again
for another 70 years.

01:16:20.199 --> 01:16:22.167
Do you think that's true?

01:16:22.201 --> 01:16:25.432
It's hard to believe
it's possible.

01:16:25.471 --> 01:16:28.304
What's going to happen to us?

01:16:32.011 --> 01:16:34.878
Are you going to be sad forever,
big brother?

01:16:34.914 --> 01:16:37.679
At least we're still alive,
aren't we?

01:16:37.717 --> 01:16:39.116
Don't worry, I'll catch it.

01:16:39.152 --> 01:16:40.517
Igor it!

01:16:42.488 --> 01:16:47.187
Hey, get over here.
Look what lfound! Come here!

01:16:47.227 --> 01:16:48.490
What is it?

01:16:48.528 --> 01:16:50.622
Look! Something's growing!

01:16:50.663 --> 01:16:54.293
Yeah, it's wheat!
The wheat's coming up again.

01:16:54.333 --> 01:16:58.998
Its life begins in
the coldest season of the year.

01:16:59.038 --> 01:17:02.008
The rain pounds it,
the wind blows it...

01:17:02.041 --> 01:17:04.203
it's crushed
beneath people's feet...

01:17:04.243 --> 01:17:06.575
but still, the wheat
spreads its roots and grows.

01:17:06.613 --> 01:17:08.411
It survives.

01:17:08.448 --> 01:17:10.416
Learn from it, boys.

01:17:10.450 --> 01:17:14.250
Grow big and strong
and let nothing beat you down.

01:17:14.287 --> 01:17:16.381
Can you see it, Father?

01:17:16.422 --> 01:17:18.220
The wheat's growing again.

01:17:19.759 --> 01:17:21.989
Good old wheat.

01:17:22.028 --> 01:17:23.723
Nothing could kill it.

01:17:23.763 --> 01:17:26.027
Not the fires, rain,
or diseases. Nothing.

01:17:26.065 --> 01:17:30.059
Who said it wouldn't grow
for 70 years? Ha ha!

01:17:30.103 --> 01:17:31.229
What a stupid!

01:17:31.270 --> 01:17:33.967
Hey, what's happening
to your head?

01:17:34.006 --> 01:17:38.034
My hair! I can feel it.
My hair's growing back again.

01:17:38.077 --> 01:17:40.239
Hey, maybe Tomoko gave you
all her hair when she died.

01:17:40.279 --> 01:17:41.747
You think?

01:17:41.781 --> 01:17:44.842
- My hair. Tomoko?
- She won't be needing it.

01:17:44.884 --> 01:17:46.716
Yeah, maybe you're right,
little brother.

01:17:46.753 --> 01:17:49.450
This way I'll always have
part of her with me forever.

01:17:49.489 --> 01:17:53.255
Isn't it great?
The wheat's growing...

01:17:53.292 --> 01:17:55.420
your hair's growing,
and even...

01:17:55.461 --> 01:17:57.793
No. Nothing down there yet.

01:17:57.830 --> 01:17:59.491
You idiot!

01:17:59.532 --> 01:18:01.796
I'm going to tell Mother!

01:18:04.003 --> 01:18:07.769
Don't worry, Father.
I'll never give up.

01:18:07.807 --> 01:18:09.832
I'll grow up big and strong...

01:18:09.875 --> 01:18:11.536
and you'll be proud of me,
you'll see.

01:18:14.247 --> 01:18:17.774
Come right home
after school, OK, big brother?

01:18:17.817 --> 01:18:19.945
Don't forget, OK?

01:18:19.986 --> 01:18:22.751
'Cause we're going down
the river, right? You promise?

01:18:31.497 --> 01:18:34.125
What's that you're making,
Gen, a boat?

01:18:34.167 --> 01:18:35.328
Yeah.

01:18:40.573 --> 01:18:43.804
OK, Shinji,
here's your boat. You ready?

01:18:43.843 --> 01:18:46.676
We're finally going to put it
in the river like we said.

01:18:54.587 --> 01:18:56.282
You ready, Ryuta?

01:18:56.322 --> 01:18:57.448
Ready!

01:18:57.490 --> 01:18:58.616
How about you, Mother? Ready?

01:18:58.658 --> 01:18:59.819
Ready.
